G4413G.def:
B. Superl., πρῶτος, -η, -ον, 
[in LXX chiefly for רִאשׁוֹן, also for אֶחַד, etc. ;] 
first, 
__1. of Time or Place; 
__(a) absol., as subst., ὁ π.., Luc 14:18, Jean 19:32, 1 Corinthiens 14:30; ὁ π. καὶ ὁ ἔσχατος, Apocalypse 1:17 2:8 22:13; neut., τὸ π., opposite to τ. δεύτερον, Hébreux 10:9; τὰ π., opposite to τ. ἔσχατα, Matthieu 12:45, Luc 11:26, 2 Pierre 2:20; anarth., Matthieu 10:2; pl., Matthieu 19:30, Marc 10:31, Luc 13:30; ἐν πρώτοις (EV, first of all), 1 Corinthiens 15:3; 
__(b) as adj.: πρώτῃ; (sc. ἡμέρᾳ) σαββάτου, Mk 16:[9]; φυλακή, opposite to δευτέρα, Actes 12:10; equiv. to adv. in English, Jhn.8:[7] 20:4, 8 Actes 27:43, Romains 10:19, 1 Timothée 1:16, 1 Jean 4:19; = πρότερος (see infr.; cf. M, Pr., 79; Bl, §11, 5; Thackeray, Gr., 183f.): with genitive, π. μου ἦν (my chief: Abbott, Jg., 509ff.; but cf. M, Pr., 245), Jean 1:15, 30; with art., Marc 14:12, Actes 1:1, al.; before ὁ δεύτερος, etc., Matthieu 22:25, Marc 12:20, al. 
__2. Of Rank or Dignity, chief, principal: Matthieu 20:27 22:38, Marc 9:35, Éphésiens 6:2, al.; with genitive, Marc 12:28, 29 al.; πόλις (Field, Notes, 124), Actes 16:12; with art., Luc 15:22 19:47, Actes 13:50, al. 
__3. Neut., πρῶτον, as adv., first, at the first; 
__(a) of Time: Matthieu 8:21, Marc 4:28, al.; τὸ π., Jean 10:40, al.; 
__(b) of Order: Romains 3:2, 1 Corinthiens 11:18, al.

