G4430.def:
πτῶμα -τος, τό
(πίπτω), [in LXX: Juges 14:8 (מַפֶּלֶת), Job 16:15 (14) (פֶּרֶץ), Ésaïe 51:19 (שֹׁד), Jdth.8:19, Wis.4:18, al. ;] 
__1. a fall, metaphorically, a misfortune, calamity (Trag., Plat., Polyb., al.; LXX). 
__2. That which has fallen; 
__(a) of buildings, a ruin (Polyb.); 
__(b) of living creatures, in cl. (poët. only) usually with genitive, νεκρῶν, etc., but also absol., as in late writers and NT, a fallen body, a carcase, corpse: Matthieu 14:12 24:28, Marc 15:45; π. αὐτοῦ, Marc 6:29; αὐτῶν, Apocalypse 11:8-9 (cf. Rutherford, NPhr., 472 f.).†

G4464.def:
ῥάβδος, -ου, ἡ 
[in LXX chiefly for מַטֶּה (e.g. Genèse 47:31, MT, מַטֶּה, bed), also for מַקֵּל, שֵׁבֶט, etc. ;] 
a staff, rod: Hébreux 9:4, Apocalypse 11:1; in particular, 
__(a) a staff, such as is used on a journey: Matthieu 10:10, Marc 6:8, Luc 9:3, Hébreux 11:21" (LXX) ; 
__(b) a ruler's staff, a sceptre: Hébreux 1:8 (LXX) Apocalypse 2:27 12:5 19:15; 
__(with) a rod for chastisement (cf. ῥαβδίζω): ἐν ῥ. (see: ἐν): 1 Corinthiens 4:21.†

G4465.def:
ῥαβδοῦχος, -ου, ό
(ῥαβδος, ἔχω), 
one who carries a rod or staff of office; 
__(a) an umpire or judge (Plat.); 
__(b) in late writers, a Roman lictor: Actes 16:38.†

G4491.def:
ῥίζα, -ης, ἡ 
[in LXX chiefly for שָׁרַשׁ ;] 
a root: Matthieu 3:10, Luc 3:9; ἐκ ῥιζῶν, Marc 11:20; ῥ. ἔχειν, Matthieu 13:6, Marc 4:6; id. before ἐν ἑαυτῷ, figuratively, Matthieu 13:21, Marc 4:17, Luc 8:13. Metaphorical (as in various senses in cl.), of cause, origin, source, etc.; 
__(a) of things, ῥ. πάντων τ. κακῶν (Eur.), 1 Timothée 6:10; 
__(b) of persons: of ancestors, Romains 11:16-18; ῥ. πικρίας, Hébreux 12:15. Of that which springs from a root, a shoot; metaphorically, of offspring, Romains 15:12 (LXX) Apocalypse 5:5 22:16.†
